# Start: a transfer page, focus on SAVES. End: same page, focus on ROMS AND
# BIOS, its switch flipped. Flip, not set: the row remembers its last state.
#
# The switch press takes `wait-for-change <timeout> 0` -- no re-send. A
# toggle is the one press where the tool's default retry would be wrong:
# pressing it a second time puts the switch back, so an eaten press must be
# reported rather than repaired. A flipped switch moves about 0.2% of the
# screen, twice the tool's threshold and seven times the clock's tick.
key down
wait-for-change
key x
wait-for-change 12 0
settle
shot roms-flipped
key up
wait-for-change
